00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.280
So looking at our goals,
as for our organization,

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.350
we have three things
that we try to mention.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.840
It's anticipate, plan and transform.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.470
So the anticipatory part is to
focus on all the early action

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:00.270
and being out early and
to be able to understand

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.110
what is going to happen

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.950
when it comes to climate-forced
migration and displacement,

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.650
also to refer to as climate mobility.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.970
Then based on that information

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.100
that we get through the
knowledge work that we do,

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.710
we then try to convene policy
makers and stakeholders

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:17.403
in different convenings
to plan for what's ahead.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:21.120
With that information and
with those coalitions,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.940
then looking at how we
can guide adaptation work

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.653
and also work with the development
planning and investments

00:05:26.653 --> 00:05:30.570
to address this in
climate mobility hotspots.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:32.610
We'll come back to this notion of hotspots

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:34.710
and what that means, but that's something

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:37.163
that you'll hear quite a
lot in this presentation.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.390
So how do we do this

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.770
when we're trying to address these goals?

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.590
We build knowledge, we advance policy

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:46.440
and we accelerate diplomacy
and enable practice.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.390
Big words, but we try to live up to them.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:51.000
We try to do various things within them.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.850
Sarah, as you heard in
the interaction from Tony,

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.250
is leading our knowledge
work that really focus

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:59.490
on how the frontline communities
are gonna be affected

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:00.480
during the climate crisis

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.790
and what that's gonna do for mobility.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.470
Based on that information,

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.780
we're then trying to advance coalitions

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:11.400
when it comes to policy to
take action, achieve justice,

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.530
and also then advance in
these different fields

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.540
that you see about outlined
peace building development,

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.073
et cetera in the policy area.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.570
How this is done as well is
through accelerating diplomacy.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:24.810
We come from the UN after all
and we work in that space.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.205
So we have something to do with diplomacy.

00:06:27.205 --> 00:06:28.917
This is a picture from last week.

00:06:28.917 --> 00:06:30.840
Actually, both these
pictures are from last week,

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.610
but that's John Kerry
and this the president

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.370
of the UN general assembly
at ourC-level rise summit

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.870
that we had last first day.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.820
So see how can we foster narratives

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.770
and advance climate mobility

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:44.220
in the international diplomatic space?

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.980
And also back to Sarah,
when it comes to practice,

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.370
how can we foster community
of practice around the world

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.420
that works on these topics?

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.593
We'll come back to this a bit more as well

00:06:52.593 --> 00:06:54.750
when we look at the different initiatives

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.750
and what we do in the different regions.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:00.900
So looking at the regional
models that we are using

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.500
for these different initiatives.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.970
So we're working towards
people-centered climate action.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.740
We can talk about mitigation,

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.810
we can talk about different
things that we need to do

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.678
because to tackle the climate crisis,

00:07:14.678 --> 00:07:16.107
but we are also trying to bring back

00:07:16.107 --> 00:07:18.570
the people into this
discussion and that's central

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:20.720
when you talk about
mobility and migration.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.240
So it is a joint undertaking
and that's something we say,

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:25.547
we're UN, this and that,

00:07:25.547 --> 00:07:27.510
but we also work with the World Bank

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:28.770
and regional organizations.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.330
It's always anchor regional,

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.400
regional organization in Africa.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.690
The African Union in the Great
Caribbean is the Association

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:36.993
of Caribbean States.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:42.030
So tying back into these
things that we discussed

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.590
in the previous slides on the approach,

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:46.620
we are purchasing an
evidence-based approach.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.870
We're also trying to
generate political momentum

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:52.920
through this coalition
building and agendas.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:56.580
And then that hopefully leads to action

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.010
that is people-centered and
takes people into account

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.110
when we're trying to
tackle the climate crisis

00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:04.692
and when we try to address
migration across these regions.

00:08:04.692 --> 00:08:07.380
And I should say that
it, we work across these,

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:09.780
you see these different
terms here, climate action,

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.030
migration displacement and
sustainable development.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:14.712
Three different agendas that operate

00:08:14.712 --> 00:08:16.110
in the international space

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:19.593
that we're all trying to bind
together in these initiatives.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.050
So how we're trying to do this
is that we are doing modeling

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:27.480
of people and population
modeling and migration modeling

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.670
of how people are foreseen to be moving

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:33.420
the future based on different
data sets, crop yield,

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:36.510
water availability, migration patterns,

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.520
other things that are have to
do with with climate change

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.560
and how this gonna affect people.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.780
I'm not gonna go into RCPs, SSPs,

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:44.910
there's beautiful information
online and Sarah might mention

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.380
a little bit about that.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.610
But they're basically

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:50.070
how you set up these different
scenarios for the future

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:52.820
in terms of development and
also in terms of emissions.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.460
And, yeah, we do this up until 2050

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.440
to get a pretty good picture down

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:02.460
to really granular information
on how that will look

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:04.983
in the different regions after 2050.

00:09:07.263 --> 00:09:09.960
We also couple this with
looking at, here it comes again,

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.300
hotspots, we'll go into this hotspots

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.850
to conduct qualitative
research through partners

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:17.280
and people in our network.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.800
So we're looking at, for
example, here are the regions

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:21.420
in Africa that we have
gone to and done this.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:24.660
You'll see Lagos, you see
Guana, you see Beira, et cetera,

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.430
where we have done focus
groups and interviews

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:29.070
to get a better understanding
of what's behind these numbers

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:31.143
that we see in the modeling work.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:33.900
So both seeing what's happening right now

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:37.050
but also seeing people's
outlooks for the future,

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.700
which Sarah will talk more about.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.210
Then this leads to consultations.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:45.030
So we conducted a
consultation process in Africa

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.740
and we will do one
degree Caribbean as well.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:49.350
The one in Africa had over
700 entities participating

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.790
in different formats.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:54.090
Everything from community
members, academia,

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.550
policy makers, NGOs.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.260
I think we even had private
sector in some of them.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:01.888
So we covered quite a lot of
stakeholder groups in there.

00:10:01.888 --> 00:10:06.390
So these also leads to the
creation of an Agenda for Action

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:07.713
which we'll get back to,

00:10:08.724 --> 00:10:12.540
but it basically is this bridge
between the modeling data,

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:15.953
the information from the qualitative work

00:10:15.953 --> 00:10:17.790
and how we can analyze that

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:21.030
and turn it into something
that's actionable.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:22.590
We also have stakeholder forums

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.570
and engage with different constituencies.

00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:26.460
I, as you heard in the introduction,

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.020
work particularly with youth.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.090
And there we have, especially since

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:32.310
that's the most advanced
advanced initiative,

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.360
a very vibrant African youth network

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:40.370
that is working across different
parts of our initiatives.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:42.030
